This repository includes third-party code, vendored verbatim as example
programs. Each such file keeps its original header, which records its
provenance and license, and stays under that license.

Python tier:

- Examples/python/bench_bisect/bench_bisect.py
- Examples/python/bench_heapq_sift/bench_heapq_sift.py
- Examples/python/bench_statistics/bench_statistics.py
    Functions from the CPython 3.9 standard library (bisect, heapq,
    statistics). Copyright (c) 2001-2026 Python Software Foundation.
    Python Software Foundation License Version 2 (SPDX: PSF-2.0).

- Examples/python/rsa_inverse/rsa_inverse.py
    Functions from python-rsa 4.9.1 (rsa/common.py).
    Copyright 2011 Sybren A. Stuvel. Apache License 2.0.

Other tiers (research in progress, not part of the Python 0.1.0 release):

- Examples/system-verilog/sem2/*/cv32e40p_*.sv
    From the OpenHW Group CV32E40P core. Copyright 2018 ETH Zurich and
    University of Bologna. Solderpad Hardware License 0.51 (SHL-0.51).
- Examples/go/*/guards.lean, where they quote Go functions
    From the Go 1.25.6 runtime and standard library. Copyright 2009 The Go
    Authors. BSD-3-Clause.

The generated *.json envelopes next to these files are syntax trees of
the same programs and carry the same licenses.
